# Claude Code: personal + transient state is local; SHARED project config
# (.claude/settings.json, commands/, agents/, skills/) is tracked when it is added.
# settings.local.json is a per-developer permission allow-list (machine-local) and must
# never be committed; worktrees/ is transient. Made explicit here so the ignore does not
# rely on a contributor's personal ~/.config/git/ignore.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.pyd
*.c
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environment
.venv/
venv/

# Testing / coverage
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
.pytest_cache/
coverage.xml

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Project notes — root .md files stay local by default. Tracked exceptions: README,
# the guardrails CLAUDE.md, the new-tree CHANGELOG.md and the debt ledger OPEN.md.
# The docs/ design workspace (artifacts + ledger + handoffs) is a sub-directory, so it
# is tracked and is NOT affected by this root /*.md anchor. Old audit ledgers, plans,
# ideas and module-health trackers remain local.
#
# REFERENCES.md and RELEASE_NOTES.md were dropped at the restart (artifact 23): the
# frozen quarry release log does not cross (CLAUDE.md §7). Their allowlist entries are
# removed so a stray file of either name is not silently tracked again.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/OPEN.md

# Local-only archive of closed audit ledgers + pre-audit historical plans.
# Moved out of repo root for visual cleanliness on 2026-06-19 after the
# v1.119 audit-chain closure. Restore from here if a future session needs
# them; nothing in archive is referenced by active code or tests.
.archive/

# Cross-surface prompt channel between Claude Code and Cowork (added 2026-10-25;
# split 2026-10-26). The two files have opposite lifetimes:
#
#   thread.md  — the CONVERSATION. Local working state, not history: untracked so it
#                cannot add commit noise to the one-slice-one-commit-one-stamp
#                sequence, and cleared when a slice closes. Decisions that matter are
#                written to docs/ and OPEN.md in the same turn.
#   README.md  — the PROTOCOL Cowork obeys. TRACKED. It cites this repo's own law
#                (§1/§4/§5/§7/§8, its doc numbers, real commit examples) and has
#                earned amendments from real failures — the re-read-before-append rule
#                (a collision wasted thread entry 0003) and the
#                working-tree-is-shared-state rule (Cowork reads the checked-out
#                branch, so a checkout changes its world). Regenerating it from the
#                generic `cowork` skill would silently discard all of that, so it is
#                repo convention, not working state.
#
# Note the form: `.cowork/*` not `.cowork/`, because git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is itself excluded.
.cowork/*
!.cowork/README.md
